<Layout
	title="Trigonometric Ratios | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Learn the six trigonometric ratios — sin, cos, tan, cosec, sec and cot — using a right-angled triangle."
>

<main class="lesson-page">

<div class="lesson-container">

<a href="/trigonometry" class="back-link">
	← Back to Trigonometry
</a>


<section class="lesson-header">

	<div class="lesson-number">
		02
	</div>

	<div>

		<div class="lesson-label">
			LESSON 02 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS
		</div>

		<h1>
			Trigonometric <span>Ratios</span>
		</h1>

		<p>
			Learn how the sides of a right-angled triangle are used
			to define the fundamental trigonometric ratios.
		</p>

	</div>

</section>


<section class="content-layout">


<article class="lesson-content">


<div class="topic-label">
01 · THE BASICS
</div>


<h2>
What are Trigonometric Ratios?
</h2>


<p>
Trigonometric ratios are ratios of the sides of a
right-angled triangle with respect to a particular
acute angle.
</p>


<p>
The value of a trigonometric ratio depends on the
angle <strong>θ</strong> and the relationship between
the sides of the triangle.
</p>



<div class="idea-box">

<div class="idea-icon">
✓
</div>


<div>

<strong>
Key Idea
</strong>


<p>
Always identify Perpendicular, Base and Hypotenuse
with respect to angle θ before using any formula.
</p>


</div>

</div>




<div class="topic-label second-label">
02 · IDENTIFY THE SIDES
</div>



<h2>
Find the three sides
</h2>


<p>
Before using any formula, identify the
<strong>Perpendicular</strong>,
<strong>Base</strong>
and
<strong>Hypotenuse</strong>
with respect to angle θ.
</p>



<div class="triangle-card">


<div class="triangle-visual">


<svg
viewBox="0 0 500 330"
role="img"
aria-label="Right angled triangle"
>


<polygon
points="95,265 95,75 405,265"
fill="#eef4ff"
stroke="#14213d"
stroke-width="4"
/>


<polyline
points="95,235 125,235 125,265"
fill="none"
stroke="#2563eb"
stroke-width="4"
/>


<text
x="250"
y="300"
text-anchor="middle"
class="svg-label"
>
Base
</text>


<text
x="52"
y="175"
text-anchor="middle"
class="svg-label"
transform="rotate(-90 52 175)"
>
Perpendicular
</text>


<text
x="285"
y="155"
text-anchor="middle"
class="svg-label"
transform="rotate(31 285 155)"
>
Hypotenuse
</text>


<path
d="M373 265 A32 32 0 0 1 378 249"
fill="none"
stroke="#f4c430"
stroke-width="5"
/>


<text
x="365"
y="259"
text-anchor="middle"
class="angle-label"
>
θ
</text>


</svg>


</div>



<div class="triangle-info">


<div class="side-info">

<div class="side-dot blue-dot"></div>

<div>

<strong>
Perpendicular
</strong>

<span>
Side opposite angle θ.
</span>

</div>

</div>



<div class="side-info">

<div class="side-dot yellow-dot"></div>

<div>

<strong>
Base
</strong>

<span>
Side adjacent to angle θ.
</span>

</div>

</div>



<div class="side-info">

<div class="side-dot navy-dot"></div>

<div>

<strong>
Hypotenuse
</strong>

<span>
Side opposite 90° angle.
</span>

</div>

</div>


</div>


</div>
<!-- BASIC RATIOS -->

<div class="topic-label second-label">
03 · BASIC RATIOS
</div>


<h2>
The three fundamental ratios
</h2>


<p>
The three basic trigonometric ratios are
<strong>sin θ</strong>,
<strong>cos θ</strong>
and
<strong>tan θ</strong>.
</p>



<div class="ratio-card">

<div class="ratio-number">
01
</div>


<div class="ratio-content">


<div class="ratio-title">

<span>
sin θ
</span>

<small>
Sine
</small>

</div>


<div class="formula">

<span>
sin θ
</span>

=

<span class="fraction">

<span>
Perpendicular
</span>

<span>
Hypotenuse
</span>

</span>

</div>


<p>
Sine of an angle is the ratio of Perpendicular
to Hypotenuse.
</p>


</div>

</div>




<div class="ratio-card">

<div class="ratio-number">
02
</div>


<div class="ratio-content">


<div class="ratio-title">

<span>
cos θ
</span>

<small>
Cosine
</small>

</div>


<div class="formula">

<span>
cos θ
</span>

=

<span class="fraction">

<span>
Base
</span>

<span>
Hypotenuse
</span>

</span>

</div>


<p>
Cosine of an angle is the ratio of Base
to Hypotenuse.
</p>


</div>

</div>




<div class="ratio-card">

<div class="ratio-number">
03
</div>


<div class="ratio-content">


<div class="ratio-title">

<span>
tan θ
</span>

<small>
Tangent
</small>

</div>


<div class="formula">

<span>
tan θ
</span>

=

<span class="fraction">

<span>
Perpendicular
</span>

<span>
Base
</span>

</span>

</div>


<p>
Tangent of an angle is the ratio of Perpendicular
to Base.
</p>


</div>

</div>





<!-- REMEMBER -->


<div class="remember-card">


<div class="remember-icon">
!
</div>


<div>

<span>
REMEMBER
</span>


<strong>
Always identify the sides with respect to the angle θ.
</strong>


</div>


</div>





<!-- SOH CAH TOA -->


<div class="topic-label second-label">
04 · QUICK MEMORY
</div>


<h2>
Remember SOH-CAH-TOA
</h2>


<p>
A simple way to remember the three basic
trigonometric ratios is
<strong>SOH-CAH-TOA</strong>.
</p>



<div class="memory-grid">


<div class="memory-card">

<div class="memory-word">
SOH
</div>

<strong>
Sin θ
</strong>

<span>
Perpendicular / Hypotenuse
</span>

</div>




<div class="memory-card">

<div class="memory-word">
CAH
</div>

<strong>
Cos θ
</strong>

<span>
Base / Hypotenuse
</span>

</div>




<div class="memory-card">

<div class="memory-word">
TOA
</div>

<strong>
Tan θ
</strong>

<span>
Perpendicular / Base
</span>

</div>


</div>





<!-- PRACTICE -->


<div class="topic-label second-label">
05 · PRACTICE PROBLEMS
</div>


<h2>
Test Your Understanding
</h2>



<div class="example-card">


<div class="example-header">

<span class="example-badge">
EXAMPLE 1
</span>


<h3>
Calculating Trigonometric Ratios
</h3>


</div>



<div class="example-solution">

<p>
In a right triangle, Perpendicular = 6 cm,
Base = 8 cm and Hypotenuse = 10 cm.
Find sin θ, cos θ and tan θ.
</p>


<p>
<strong>
Solution:
</strong>
</p>


<ul>

<li>
sin θ = 6/10 = <strong>3/5</strong>
</li>

<li>
cos θ = 8/10 = <strong>4/5</strong>
</li>

<li>
tan θ = 6/8 = <strong>3/4</strong>
</li>

</ul>


</div>


</div>




<div class="example-card">


<div class="example-header">

<span class="example-badge">
EXAMPLE 2
</span>


<h3>
Finding Ratios From sin A
</h3>


</div>



<div class="example-solution">

<p>
If sin A = 3/5, find cos A and tan A.
</p>


<p>
<strong>
Solution:
</strong>
</p>


<p>
Let Perpendicular = 3k and Hypotenuse = 5k.
</p>


<p>
By Pythagoras theorem:
</p>


<p>
Base = √(25k² - 9k²) = 4k
</p>


<div class="calc-box">

cos A = 4/5
<br/>
tan A = 3/4

</div>


</div>


</div>
